    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0450" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 814.01B/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leavell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-15T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received July 16, 8.18 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 12, 5 p.m. Taking over of the German properties here is entirely by
                    presidential decree and is at present limited to the four properties named in my
                    cipher telegram of July 4, 10 a.m., which are to be operated by the Custodian
                    and those net receipts going to Germans held until the war ends. At the present
                    moment nobody knows if President Cabrera intends to go beyond this point. As
                    soon as I can see him, I will ask about this and the other latest instances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leavell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
